    {
      "cve": "CVE-2026-59679",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-59679"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "fs_read_glyphs() in the libXfont2 font-server client (src/fc/fserve.c) indexes the per-character encoding[] array using num_chars from the FS_QueryXBitmaps16 reply, but that array was allocated with a size derived from num_extents in the separate FS_QueryXExtents16 reply. The two CARD32 fields are never cross-checked.\nA malicious or compromised font server can send a small num_extents (e.g. 1) in the extents reply, then a large num_chars (e.g. 100000) in the bitmaps reply. This causes attacker-controlled out-of-bounds heap read and writes.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
      "product_status": {
        "recommended": [
          "openSUSE Leap 16.0:libXfont2-2-0:2.0.7-160000.5.1.aarch64",
